+// keepEmptySeriesForExemplars reports whether a series that has no chunks left
+// must keep its identity in the head because it still has an exemplar at or
+// after the replay cutoff. Exemplars are not persisted to blocks, so the WAL
+// series record must be kept until the cutoff moves past the exemplar;
+// otherwise WAL replay finds the exemplar record but cannot resolve its series
+// reference and drops it.
+//
+// Must be called with the series lock held.
+func (h *Head) keepEmptySeriesForExemplars(s *memSeries) bool {
+	if !s.hasExemplar {
+		return false
+	}
+	// Use the minimum valid time rather than the head's minimum time: the head
+	// can be uninitialized (minimum time math.MaxInt64) after replaying only a
+	// series record and its exemplars, and it is the minimum valid time that
+	// bounds what WAL replay will accept.
+	return s.maxExemplarTime >= h.minValidTime.Load()
+}
